igned}]=i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/77936c4115b37d79ae301a93b218ecd23114ae4ad42d8298b8f058c1f50e82a2.png)\n\nSo, the matrix represents a rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians **clockwise** about the origin.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ **clockwise** by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/d5ff1c1a7c99b08d04d2ac58d9f8195ee29c8b564873a9abfb2635e93cec1968.png)" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293906 13194139534542 true] [17592186293905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293907 13194139534542 true] [17592186293905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293908 13194139534542 true] [17592186293905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293909 13194139534542 true] [17592186293905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293910 13194139534542 true] [17592186293905 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534542 true] [17592186293905 1041 "selection" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293905 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293906 13194139534542 true] [17592186293905 1110 #uuid "7099fd12-65a9-5316-9ba3-b4fd5bb3e69a" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293906 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/70dfc0c8412bfae3bdbb7128fc021199f11d63d6f4ee264bea20da70dd18316c.png" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293906 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534542 true] [17592186293906 1111 #uuid "49be66f3-ba66-5919-b1db-61bdeb019eba" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293907 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/09b2ae9333118de0621a5f29610b6a83689fadaeb9c05e7a30b2799b12a1bd58.png" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293907 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534542 true] [17592186293907 1111 #uuid "9a7d6100-079c-5012-9b5f-037a5687e6cb" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293908 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/ead70b80d9256e1211addc404613f2dfe4a19baf822cbd77f429572ffc9a3a6d.png" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293908 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534542 true] [17592186293908 1111 #uuid "708ee9ac-745d-55db-b410-f1f4aab15194" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293909 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/5a1923eec2b66ef4eb861ec42b00ea48a3285aaaf3255c42d12c001c9cde32f8.png" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534542 true] [17592186293909 1111 #uuid "3c8adda5-0333-5dd2-8fb3-c3aec8bca265" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293910 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/23f63717c8d356c698137359824112511b0bbd5ec04c59e47d22500d842d03b6.png" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293910 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534542 true] [17592186293910 1111 #uuid "5bbcd6fb-ec6e-579f-beca-1eaad44b5f89" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293911 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293912 13194139534542 true] [17592186293911 1089 "q-160644" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293911 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534542 true] [17592186293911 1100 "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(2,-3),(3,1),(-4,-1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{270}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${270}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(3,2)$\n- $(1,-3)$\n- $(-1,4)$" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293911 1113 #uuid "8d8905ff-87fc-56b7-a3d8-d73cbc677520" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293911 1145 "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{270}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${270}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{270}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{270}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,-2),(1,-3),(-1,4).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293913 13194139534542 true] [17592186293912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293914 13194139534542 true] [17592186293912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293915 13194139534542 true] [17592186293912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293916 13194139534542 true] [17592186293912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293917 13194139534542 true] [17592186293912 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534542 true] [17592186293912 1041 "selection" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293912 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293913 13194139534542 true] [17592186293912 1110 #uuid "0e1d7e5c-861f-50ad-96f8-5c1feba4e907" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293913 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293913 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534542 true] [17592186293913 1111 #uuid "61129a8e-e817-555a-b8cc-c20f7bd58800" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293914 1034 "I only" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293914 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534542 true] [17592186293914 1111 #uuid "ad5b0ee2-7af1-5000-b95c-9787ca1087c5" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293915 1034 "III only" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293915 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534542 true] [17592186293915 1111 #uuid "317cb7f7-cd1c-5803-88fa-e4caf85faf2a" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293916 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534542 true] [17592186293916 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534542 true] [17592186293916 1111 #uuid "b5f75dfa-b784-5059-a491-313dfb65c162" 131941395345